    :relationships,
    :reviews,
    :status,
    :status_market,
    :updated_at,
    :workflow
  ]

  @typedoc """
  * `decisions`: Every decision taken on the case, oldest first.
  * `documents`: The documents and selfies of the case with the reviewers' decision about each, oldest first, as GET /v1/cases/{id}/documents lists them.
  * `kind` (one of `"KYC"`, `"KYB"`, `"AGE"`)
  * `livemode`: False when the answer comes from the organization's sandbox: synthetic data, engine doubles chosen by the documented magic values, nothing billed and no official source consulted. True in production.
  * `status` (one of `"open"`, `"processing"`, `"awaiting_input"`, `"in_review"`, `"approved"`, `"rejected"`, `"cancelled"`, `"expired"`)
  * `status_market` (one of `"PROCESSING"`, `"PENDING_OCR"`, `"PENDING"`, `"APPROVED"`, `"REPROVED"`, `"BLOCKED"`, `"CANCELLED"`, `"EXPIRED"`): The status in the vocabulary of the Brazilian KYC market, beside status, which keeps its values: PROCESSING (open, processing, awaiting_input), PENDING_OCR (in_review because a document reading check -- OCR or validation -- failed or timed out), PENDING (in_review, waiting for a human decision), APPROVED (approved), REPROVED (rejected), BLOCKED (rejected by the policy's block outcome, such as a confirmed sanctions match), CANCELLED (cancelled) and EXPIRED (expired). CANCELLED and EXPIRED are closed without a decision. It never changes the decision.
  * `workflow`: The workflow run and its steps, or null before the case starts.
  """
  @type t :: %__MODULE__{
          checks: [Kuaa.Check.t()],
          created_at: String.t(),
          current_state: String.t(),
          decisions: [Kuaa.Decision.t()],
